{"judge_label": "committed_silent", "justification_span": "Male, creatinine 1.84 mg/dL, age 64.\n\n2021 CKD-EPI (no race):\nFor males, creatinine > 0.9: use κ=0.9, exponent -1.200.\n\nGFR = 142 × (Scr/0.9)^(-1.200) × 0.9938^age\n\nScr/κ = 1.84/0.9 = 2.0444\n(2.0444)^(-1.200):\nln(2.0444) = 0.7152\n× -1.200 = -0.8583\ne^(-0.8583) = 0.4238\n\n0.9938^64:\nln(0.9938) = -0.006219\n× 64 = -0.398\ne^(-0.398) = 0.6716\n\nGFR = 142 × 0.4238 × 0.6716\n= 142 × 0.2846 = 40.4\n\nFINAL: 40"}